--- a/MODEM_REFERENCE_RECEIVER.md
+++ b/MODEM_REFERENCE_RECEIVER.md
@@ -82,3 +82,25 @@ feed boundaries, gaps, changed gain, fresh frames, erased headers, noise and res
 plus the existing progressive checks. Short 0.8x inspection also recovered a
 verified frame. No full suite, hardware benchmark, broad impairment sweep,
 independent-pitch validation or tape experiment was run.
+
+## Faster-playback reference correction
+
+The original wideband linear timing fit could reject a valid preamble at 1.12x:
+its sample-rounded edges put the high-frequency waveform outside the accurate
+range of a first-order correction. The reference receiver now applies one fixed,
+symmetric 33-tap low-pass FIR to both the known preamble model and the observation.
+The cached model filters the gain, delay and dilation columns consistently.
+Only the preamble timing measurement is filtered; training and payload samples
+retain their existing path.
+
+This still performs one direct solve per reference event pair. The residual
+limit remains 0.35; there are no alternative rates, correlation searches,
+iterative corrections or payload retries. Sampling, display deadlines and
+shared-time scheduling are unchanged.
+
+The added regression checks 1.12x at two input alignments, blocks calls into
+search/replay APIs, checks one reference fit and one FFT per symbol, and compares
+image error against the older progressive receiver on the same input. Existing
+normal/slow-speed, noise, reset, gap and header-erasure checks remain in place.
+This fixes the reproduced rejection, not independent pitch or all faster-input
+impairments; high carriers can still be lost near the audio Nyquist limit.
